  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Shock-Responsive Social Protection (SRSP)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will be implemented in Chikun and Kaduna North LGAs. These LGAs have continued to experience flooding incidents, with Chikun LGA having the highest number of affected individuals. Kaduna North experience devastating floods that washed away farmlands and affected over 1,000 people. Chikun LGA recorded the highest number of affected persons, with 10,115 individuals representing 27% of the affected population in the state. Houses of the affected population were either partially or completely damaged. Floods continuously have affected the people economically, caused displacement and affected livelihoods, with people relying on crop and vegetable farming, petty trade, and casual labor. Hence, this project adopt a local-government wide coverage. While CAID had working experience and established stakeholders in these LGAs, UNICEF has also invested in cash distribution to flood victims in some communities of the 2 LGAs; Hence the project will support impact evaluation of this investment with regards to early warning and households mitigation plans to flooding disaster while also strengthening capacities</narrative>
  </description>
